.TH MACHCTL 1 "October 2026" "Mach 0.9.0" "Machctl Manual"
.SH NAME
machctl \- administrative control plane for Mach Linux machines, containers, and Kubernetes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B machctl
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B machctl
is the complete management and orchestration CLI for \fBMach\fR, providing comprehensive controls for Linux virtual machines, OCI container integration, Kubernetes clusters, Apple Silicon Rosetta 2 translation, networking, and system diagnostics.

.SH LINUX MACHINE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI create " [" options "] [" name "]"
Create a new Linux virtual machine.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-d " " distro ", " \-\-distro " " distro
Linux distribution (\fIdebian\fR, \fIubuntu\fR, \fIfedora\fR, \fIalpine\fR). Defaults to \fIdebian\fR.
.TP
.BI \-c " " cpus ", " \-\-cpus " " cpus
Number of virtual CPUs (defaults to 2).
.TP
.BI \-m " " memory ", " \-\-memory " " memory
Memory allocation in MiB (defaults to 2048 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-s " " disk ", " \-\-disk " " disk
Virtual disk size in GiB (defaults to 20 GiB). APFS Copy-on-Write ensures only written blocks consume actual disk space.
.RE

.TP
.BI list ", " ls
List all configured Linux machines with their distribution, runtime status, CPU/memory usage, and IP addresses.

.TP
.BI start " [" name "]"
Boot a stopped virtual machine into the background.

.TP
.BI stop " [" name "] [" \-\-force "]"
Gracefully shut down a running machine (or immediately terminate with \fB\-\-force\fR).

.TP
.BI restart " [" name "]"
Restart a running virtual machine.

.TP
.BI delete ", " rm " [" name "] [" \-\-force "]"
Delete a virtual machine and its associated APFS disk image.

.TP
.BI clone " " source " " target
Instantly clone a machine using native APFS Copy-on-Write. Takes less than 1 millisecond and consumes zero additional disk space until modified.

.TP
.BI rename " " old_name " " new_name
Rename an existing machine.

.TP
.BI info " [" name "]"
Display detailed JSON or tabular metadata for a machine (IP address, MAC address, vCPUs, RAM, disk allocation, APFS physical footprint).

.TP
.BI top " [" interval "]"
Interactive live terminal dashboard displaying guest CPU usage, resident memory (RSS), APFS CoW disk savings, and host resource utilization.

.TP
.BI ssh " [" name "]"
Display SSH connection credentials and helper commands for a machine.

.TP
.BI push " [" \-m " " machine "] " source " " destination
Copy files or directories from macOS to the Linux guest.

.TP
.BI pull " [" \-m " " machine "] " source " " destination
Copy files or directories from the Linux guest to macOS.

.TP
.BI export " " machine " " output_archive
Export a machine's disk and metadata to a compressed \fB.tar.gz\fR archive.

.TP
.BI import " " input_archive " [" name "]"
Import a previously exported machine archive.

.TP
.BI default " [" name "]"
Get or set the active default machine used by \fBmach\fR.

.TP
.BI mount " [" name "] [" path "]"
Mount a Linux machine's filesystem or open it in macOS Finder (\fB~/Mach/machines/<name>\fR).

.SH CONTAINER & KUBERNETES COMMANDS
.TP
.BI docker " setup [" \-\-system "]"
Configure Docker CLI context \fBmach\fR pointing to the guest VM's Docker socket. With \fB\-\-system\fR, creates a system-wide symlink at \fB/var/run/docker.sock\fR for VS Code Dev Containers and Testcontainers.

.TP
.BI docker " status"
Display current Docker daemon status and API responsiveness.

.TP
.BI k8s " enable [" \-\-cpus " " N "] [" \-\-memory " " MiB "]"
Provision and start a dedicated, zero-overhead Kubernetes (K3s) node. Automatically generates and merges credentials into \fB~/.kube/config\fR without disturbing existing contexts.

.TP
.BI k8s " disable"
Stop and shut down the local Kubernetes node.

.TP
.BI k8s " status"
Display Kubernetes cluster health and node status.

.TP
.BI debug " " container_name
Drop an interactive debugging shell into a Docker container with preloaded networking and diagnostic utilities.

.SH NETWORKING & SYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.BI doctor
Run comprehensive health checks on virtualization hardware, entitlements, APFS CoW support, SSH keys, Docker sockets, and DNS resolvers.

.TP
.BI dns " setup"
Configure the native macOS resolver for \fB*.mach.local\fR domains via \fB/etc/resolver/mach.local\fR.

.TP
.BI tls " install [" \-\-system "]"
Generate and trust a local wildcard TLS certificate authority in the macOS Keychain for trusted HTTPS across browsers and curl.

.TP
.BI daemon " start | stop | status"
Manage the background async port forwarding and DNS routing daemon.

.TP
.BI uninstall " [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-force "] [" \-\-keep\-data "]"
Completely uninstall Mach, stop all VMs and daemons, reset Docker and Kubernetes contexts, restore ~/.ssh/config, remove TLS certificates, and clean up ~/.mach data.

.TP
.BI version
Print version, build profile, and target architecture.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Create an Ubuntu machine with 4 vCPUs and 4 GB RAM
machctl create --distro ubuntu --cpus 4 --memory 4096 dev-box
.TP
.B Instant APFS CoW clone of an existing machine
machctl clone dev-box dev-box-backup
.TP
.B Launch Kubernetes cluster
machctl k8s enable
.TP
.B Verify system health
machctl doctor

